  "notes": "Single decodable style (page Styles 1a-1d, one shared system): 4-character Production/Plant Code, then the 3-character Manufacture Date code at normalized positions 5-7 (1-based) / [4,7] 0-based half-open, then Production Run Number and Part Number. The page states the date is always the 5th-7th characters regardless of dash locations or omission, and the four page sample serials confirm this on the normalized (dash-stripped) serial: each yields a chart code. Chart transcribed firsthand from the page's chart image (Bosch-date-chart-1.jpg, 1173x1054) on 2026-10-28; all 252 cells legible in enlarged bands, no cell guessed; 21 year-rows (2010-2030) x 12 months, every (year, month) pair covered exactly once. Chart quirks transcribed as printed, not smoothed: 2010-2013 run sequentially (e.g. 2013: 301-312), but 2014-2029 split each year into Jan-Apr (?17-?20) and May-Dec (?53-?60) with a jump between April and May (e.g. 2014: Apr 420, May 453); 2030 switches to alphanumeric codes 0A1-0AC. Page Styles 2 (63036333-00-7080-3241) and 3 (253000-08217-01241-7747019703) are HELD, NOT SHIPPED: the page states it cannot determine the year for either; both are pre-2010 legacy systems. Page header names related brands Bosch, Buderus, FHP, Chromalox, Worcester and parent Bosch Thermotechnology Corp. (described as a subsidiary of Advanced Thermal Technologies), but the page does not document those brands sharing this code system, so no sisters are claimed. Example decodes are derived, not stated on the page: the page gives the sample serials and the chart but no worked year/month for them; each expected value below is the chart entry for that serial's 5th-7th code, verified against the chart image.",
